pageType: content
notes: |
  Scientific basis slide. Examines the foundational reaction physics of Deuterium-Tritium (D-T) fusion, the derivation of the Lawson triple product criterion, and the critical distinction between scientific plasma gain (Q_plasma) and engineering net electric gain (Q_eng). Emphasizes that commercial grid power requires Q_plasma of 25 to 40 to overcome thermal conversion Carnot limits and cryogenic magnet auxiliary loads.
elements:
  # Header Kicker
  - elementId: kicker
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 26, 600, 16]
    content:
      style: "$kicker"
      text: "01 · SCIENTIFIC BASIS"

  # Header Title
  - elementId: title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 42, 860, 30]
    content:
      style: "$title"
      text: "Lawson Criterion Defines Ignition Boundary; Scientific Gain Must Precede Engineering Net Power"

  # Header Subtitle
  - elementId: subtitle
    elementType: text
    bounds: [50, 72, 860, 16]
    content:
      style: "$subtitle"
      text: "Governing fusion cross-sections, energy release fractions, and the fundamental distinction between plasma and plant gain"

  # Header Divider
  - elementId: header-line
    elementType: line
    bounds: [50, 92, 860, 1]
    points: "0,0 860,0"
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  # Panel 1 - Reaction Physics
  - elementId: p1-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p1-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$titleNavy"}

  - elementId: p1-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "REACTION ENERGETICS & FUEL CYCLE"

  - elementId: p1-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [58, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>D-T Reaction:</b> \( \mathrm{D} + \mathrm{T} \rightarrow {^4\mathrm{He}}\,(3.52\,\mathrm{MeV}) + n\,(14.06\,\mathrm{MeV}) \)</p>
        <p><br><b>Energy Partition:</b></p>
        <p>• <b>Alpha Particle (20%):</b> Carries 3.52 MeV; electrically charged, trapped by magnetic field to provide internal plasma self-heating.</p>
        <p>• <b>Neutron (80%):</b> Carries 14.06 MeV; uncharged, penetrates first wall into breeding blanket to deposit thermal heat and breed tritium.</p>
        <p><br><b>Aneutronic Alternatives (p-¹¹B, D-³He):</b></p>
        <p>Eliminates neutron activation, but requires ion temperatures &gt;100 keV (&gt;1 billion K), where Bremsstrahlung radiation losses severely constrain net gain.</p>

  # Panel 2 - Lawson Criterion
  - elementId: p2-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [342, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p2-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [342, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$accentBlue"}

  - elementId: p2-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [350, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "THE LAWSON TRIPLE PRODUCT"

  - elementId: p2-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [350, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Ignition Criterion:</b> \( n \cdot T \cdot \tau_E \ge 3 \times 10^{21} \, \mathrm{keV}\cdot\mathrm{s}\cdot\mathrm{m}^{-3} \)</p>
        <p><br><b>Key Plasma Variables:</b></p>
        <p>• <b>\( n \) (Density):</b> Number of fuel ions per unit volume (~10²⁰ m⁻³ for MCF; ~10³¹ m⁻³ for ICF).</p>
        <p>• <b>\( T \) (Temperature):</b> Optimal reaction cross-section at 10–20 keV (~100–200 million °C).</p>
        <p>• <b>\( \tau_E \) (Confinement Time):</b> Rate of energy thermal leakage from the core plasma.</p>
        <p><br><b>Confinement Dichotomy:</b></p>
        <p>Magnetic approaches pursue high \( \tau_E \) (seconds) at low density; inertial approaches compress fuel to astronomical density for nanoseconds.</p>

  # Panel 3 - Gain Hierarchy
  - elementId: p3-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [634, 106, 276, 268]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: p3-header
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [634, 106, 276, 28]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$titleNavy"}

  - elementId: p3-title
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 111, 260, 18]
    content:
      fontSize: 9
      bold: true
      color: "$white"
      text: "GAIN HIERARCHY: PLASMA VS PLANT"

  - elementId: p3-content
    elementType: text
    bounds: [642, 142, 260, 216]
    content:
      fontSize: 8.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.35
      text: |
        <p><b>Scientific Gain:</b> \( Q_{\mathrm{plasma}} = \frac{P_{\mathrm{fusion}}}{P_{\mathrm{heat,in}}} \)</p>
        <p>• \( Q = 1 \): Scientific break-even (JET 1997: 0.67; NIF 2022: 1.54 target gain).</p>
        <p>• \( Q = \infty \): True ignition (alpha self-heating balances losses).</p>
        <p><br><b>Engineering Plant Gain:</b></p>
        <p>• \( Q_{\mathrm{eng}} = \frac{P_{\mathrm{elec,gross}}}{P_{\mathrm{recirc}}} &gt; 1 \)</p>
        <p><br><b>The Commercial Multiplier:</b></p>
        <p>Because thermal conversion efficiency is 35–45% and auxiliary systems (magnets, cryogenics, heating) consume recirculating power, a commercial power station requires \( Q_{\mathrm{plasma}} \ge 25 - 40 \).</p>

  # Watch Indicators Band
  - elementId: watch-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 384, 860, 74]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$cardBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: watch-accent
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 384, 4, 74]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$orangeAccent"}

  - elementId: watch-label
    elementType: text
    bounds: [64, 398, 118, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      bold: true
      color: "$titleNavy"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p>WATCH INDICATORS</p>
        <p>2026–2030</p>

  - elementId: watch-1
    elementType: text
    bounds: [190, 398, 250, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Demonstrated plasma gain</b></p>
        <p>0.67 (JET 1997) → 1.54 target gain (NIF 2022)</p>

  - elementId: watch-2
    elementType: text
    bounds: [450, 398, 240, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Ion temperature (keV)</b></p>
        <p>10–20 keV peak D-T cross-section; p-¹¹B needs &gt;100 keV</p>

  - elementId: watch-3
    elementType: text
    bounds: [700, 398, 210, 46]
    content:
      fontSize: 7.5
      color: "$ink"
      lineHeight: 1.3
      text: |
        <p><b>Recirculating power share</b></p>
        <p>15–30% of gross generation (magnets, cryogenics, heating)</p>

  # Bottom Synthesis Strip
  - elementId: synth-bg
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 472, 860, 32]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$panelBg"}
    border: {style: solid, width: 0.8, color: "$border"}

  - elementId: synth-accent
    elementType: shape
    bounds: [50, 472, 4, 32]
    shapeName: rect
    fill: {type: solid, color: "$accentBlue"}

  - elementId: synth-text
